{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1517769-could-someone-explain-me-the-new-rules-of-arms-of-invocation-and-banishment","id":1517769,"title":"Could someone explain me the new rules of Arms of Invocation and Banishment","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-12T07:57:18-07:00","id":1517769,"title":"Could someone explain me the new rules of Arms of Invocation and Banishment","content":"I got Tome of Pentacle book, until now is great but I got really confused with the explanation of this optional rule. Could someone explain me how exactly that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T08:57:07-07:00","id":1517786,"title":"","content":"When you engage in the Duel Arcane, each turn, you can either attack or defend. In either case, you determine an appropriate Attribute and Arcanum to roll as befits the sorcery you are demonstrating in the duel. If you attack, the Arcanum you choose is called your <b>sword.</b> If you defend, the Arcanum is your <b>shield.</b> An <b>arm</b> refers to either a sword or shield.<br /> <br /> When using the Invocation and Banishment rules, you determine these things <i>secretly,</i> revealing after both characters have decided on their action that round. Then, if one character is attacking and another is defending, you compare the attacker's sword and defender's shield to the Invocation and Banishing sequences. You can read them as circles, with Banishing listing which Arcanum is best used to attack a given Arcanum, and Invocation listing which Arcanum is best used to defend against which Arcanum. It's like rock paper scissors but with a longer list.<br /> <br /> <i>RPS: </i><b>Rock \u2192 scissors \u2192 paper \u2192 rock</b><br /> <i>Invocation (shield):</i> <b>Prime \u2192 Forces \u2192 Fate \u2192 Time \u2192 Mind \u2192 Space \u2192 Spirit \u2192 Life \u2192 Death \u2192 Matter \u2192 Prime</b><br /> <i>Banishing (sword):</i> <b>Death \u2192 Time \u2192 Spirit \u2192 Forces \u2192 Mind \u2192 Matter \u2192 Fate \u2192 Life \u2192 Prime \u2192 Space \u2192 Death</b><br /> <br /> If you have one of these interactions, then the one on &quot;top&quot; (for instance, the sword of Death against the shield of Time, or the shield of Death against the sword of Matter) gets a +2 bonus.<br /> <br /> If you know two Arcana that &quot;sandwich&quot; another Arcanum in one of the cycles, you can sacrifice one of the two sandwiching Arcana as the cycle's corresponding arm. You can't use the sacrificed Arcanum as that arm in the rest of the Duel, but you get to enhance a single corresponding action, either adding a sacrificed sword as a bonus to an attack, or sacrificing a shield to close a door when defending.<br /> <br /> <i>(So, when banishing, <b>Spirit \u2192 Forces \u2192 Mind</b>\u200b means that Spirit and Mind are sandwiching Forces\u200b. That means that if you have dots in both Spirit and Mind, you can choose to sacrifice either Spirit or Mind as a sword. If you sacrifice Spirit, you can no longer make Spirit attacks in the rest of the duel, but you can add your Spirit dots as a dice bonus to one attack using a different Arcanum. Similarly, when invoking, </i><i><b>Spirit \u2192 Life \u2192 Death</b>\u200b</i> <i>means if you have dots in both Spirit and Death, you can choose to sacrifice the shield of Spirit or Death. If you sacrifice the shield of Spirit, you can no longer defend with Spirit for the rest of the duel, but you can use one successful defense using a different Arcanum to close one of your opened Doors.)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 07-12-2023, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T14:31:43-07:00","id":1517821,"title":"","content":"Oh, I get it now, thank you for clarifying! <br /> <br /> I quite liked the new rules, the sad part is that I can't see it working with changellings in crossover, like in Dark Eras 2, so in that instances, we will need to come back to the default system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26883-imortalkiller","name":"ImortalKiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T13:29:20-07:00","id":1518266,"title":"","content":"My read of it is they brought back some of the 1E flavor for Duel Arcane. Though I found the 1E explanation much easier to understand than the current version of TotP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27301-shemihazazel","name":"shemihazazel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}